(A write in EVERY branch of an if/otherwise is definite, so the branch merge
 has to carry the same rule the top level does: `Set` names no type and so
 claims nothing about the global's kind. docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #92 struck here
 as well, through the merge.)

a list called roster is [].
a boolean called crewed is true.

To 'how many'.
    Return a number, roster's length.

If crewed then,
    Set roster to ["ada"].
Otherwise,
    Set roster to ["ada", "grace", "katherine"].

Print 'how many'.
